            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.085,
            0.599,
            0.11
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "• Why are lines l and m parallel to each other?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.138,
            0.439,
            0.162
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5.8 Alternate Angles"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.17,
            0.847,
            0.21
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In Fig. 5.25, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle d"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is called the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "alternate angle",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle f ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle c"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is the alternate angle of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle e"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.393,
            0.212,
            0.602,
            0.368
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 4,
              "bbox": [
                0.393,
                0.212,
                0.602,
                0.368
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_14_image_4.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image_caption",
              "index": 5,
              "bbox": [
                0.462,
                0.374,
                0.537,
                0.39
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 5.25"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.399,
            0.847,
            0.457
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "You can find the alternate angle of a given angle, say "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle f ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " by first finding the corresponding angle of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle f ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " which is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle b"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and then finding the vertically opposite angle of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle b ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , which is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle d ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.463,
            0.259,
            0.485
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Activity 6"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.484,
            0.846,
            0.558
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In Fig. 5.25, if "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle f"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 2 0 ^ { \\circ }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " what is the measure of its alternate angle "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle d ?"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " We can find the measure of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle d"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " if we know "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle b"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " because they are vertically opposite angles. Remember, vertically opposite angles are equal."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.557,
            0.847,
            0.595
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What is the measure of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathbb { Z } b ?"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " It is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 2 0 ^ { \\circ }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " because it is the corresponding angle of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle f ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.595,
            0.44,
            0.612
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle d"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " also measures "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 2 0 ^ { \\circ } ,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.612,
            0.846,
            0.65
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In fact, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle f = \\angle b"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " irrespective of the measure of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle f ."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Why? Because "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle b"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is the corresponding angle of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "Z   f ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.65,
            0.847,
            0.704
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Similarly, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle b = \\angle d"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " irrespective of the measure of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle b"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Why? Because "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle d"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is the vertically opposite angle of ∠b. So, it must always be the "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle b ."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " case that"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.177,
            0.705,
            0.256,
            0.723
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_14_equation_13.jpg",
          "content": "\\angle f = \\angle d"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.723,
            0.847,
            0.763
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Using our understanding of corresponding angles without any measurements, we have justified that alternate angles are always equal."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.172,
            0.79,
            0.826,
            0.83
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Alternate angles formed by a transversal intersecting a pair of parallel lines are always equal to each other."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.86,
            0.846,
            0.901
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 1:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " In Fig. 5.26, parallel lines l and m are intersected by the transversal t. If "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle 6"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 3 5 ^ { \\circ }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , what are the measures of the other angles?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.449,
            0.97,
            0.55,
            0.985
          ],
